¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙYTherefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Because thou hast set thine heart as the heart of God;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¹behold, therefore I will bring strangers upon thee, the terrible of the nations: and they shall draw their swords against the beauty of thy wisdom, and they shall defile thy brightness.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙuThey shall bring thee down to the pit, and thou shalt die the deaths of them that are slain in the midst of the seas.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ„Wilt thou yet say before him that slayeth thee, I am God? but thou shalt be a man, and no God, in the hand of him that slayeth thee.¦layout ªlast_verse	„¥verse
