…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ3Moreover the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¤Son of man, take up a lamentation upon the king of Tyrus, and say unto him, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Thou sealest up the sum, full of wisdom, and perfect in beauty.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚ:Thou hast been in Eden the garden of God; every precious stone was thy covering, the sardius, topaz, and the diamond, the beryl, the onyx, and the jasper, the sapphire, the emerald, and the carbuncle, and gold: the workmanship of thy tabrets and of thy pipes was prepared in thee in the day that thou wast created.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ­Thou art the anointed cherub that covereth; and I have set thee so: thou wast upon the holy mountain of God; thou hast walked up and down in the midst of the stones of fire.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙcThou wast perfect in thy ways from the day that thou wast created, till iniquity was found in thee.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÿBy the multitude of thy merchandise they have filled the midst of thee with violence, and thou hast sinned: therefore I will cast thee as profane out of the mountain of God: and I will destroy thee, O covering cherub, from the midst of the stones of fire.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÅThine heart was lifted up because of thy beauty, thou hast corrupted thy wisdom by reason of thy brightness: I will cast thee to the ground, I will lay thee before kings, that they may behold thee.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚThou hast defiled thy sanctuaries by the multitude of thine iniquities, by the iniquity of thy traffick; therefore will I bring forth a fire from the midst of thee, it shall devour thee, and I will bring thee to ashes upon the earth in the sight of all them that behold thee.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAll they that know thee among the people shall be astonished at thee: thou shalt be a terror, and never shalt thou be any more.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ0Again the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ@Son of man, set thy face against Zidon, and prophesy against it,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙèand say, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I am against thee, O Zidon; and I will be glorified in the midst of thee: and they shall know that I am the LORD, when I shall have executed judgments in her, and shall be sanctified in her.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÁFor I will send into her pestilence, and blood into her streets; and the wounded shall be judged in the midst of her by the sword upon her on every side; and they shall know that I am the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¾And there shall be no more a pricking brier unto the house of Israel, nor any grieving thorn of all that are round about them, that despised them; and they shall know that I am the Lord GOD.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙşThus saith the Lord GOD; When I shall have gathered the house of Israel from the people among whom they are scattered, and shall be sanctified in them in the sight of the heathen, then shall they dwell in their land that I have given to my servant Jacob.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙüAnd they shall dwell safely therein, and shall build houses, and plant vineyards; yea, they shall dwell with confidence, when I have executed judgments upon all those that despise them round about them; and they shall know that I am the LORD their God.¦layout ªlast_verse